  "tibetan_transliteration": "\u0f41\u0f74\u0f0b\u0f66\u0f9f\u0f7c\u0f53\u0f0b\u0f56\u0f62\u0fa9\u0f7c\u0f53\u0f0b\u0f60\u0f42\u0fb2\u0f74\u0f66\u0f0b\u0f42\u0f61\u0f74\u0f44\u0f0b\u0f51\u0fb2\u0f74\u0f44",
  "comments": "The Abhidharma lineage found in (ID:5483) names \"khu lha sdings pa brtson 'grus g.yung drung\" between \"gar mi yon tan g.yung drung\" (ID:4234) and \"rgya rgyal bu tshul le\" (ID:4238). \r\nThe lineage in work (ID:5264) places him between \" 'gar mi yon tan g.yung drung\" (ID:4234) and both \"ra\" (ID:4237) and \"rgya\" (ID:4238).\r\n\r\nWe consider \"khu lha sdings pa\" to be the same person as \"khu ston brtson 'grus g.yung drung,\" who founded lHa sdings (ID:6701) in Yar lung.\r\n\r\nHe is also mistakenly given the name Khu ston shes rab brtson 'grus in a lineage list, but should not be confused with (ID:3823) ([TZC3JQWE]: 342).",
  "alternative_names_legacy": "khu brtson 'grus g.yung drung\r\nkhu ston chen po brtson 'grus g.yung drung\r\nkhu lha sdings pa\r\nkhu chen po lha sdings pa\r\nkhu ston shes rab brtson 'grus",
